{
 "about": "Event record files and the verdict the reader (crates/scout-corpus/src/events.rs) gives each. Run by crates/scout-corpus/tests/event_record_fixtures.rs. A control-* case holds a control character the reader refuses anywhere in a record file (events/record.rs, `has_control`); they are all made from hex, a raw NUL or CR does not sit well in git. The reader is the one implementation of the record format: `scout events seed` reads and checks records with it. verdict: accept (read as a record), reject (skipped with a warning; `why` is a phrase of that warning), ignored (not a record file). A case with `make` has no file in records/: the tests create it (pad: text then one byte repeated up to a size; repeat: prefix, a unit repeated, suffix; hex: these bytes; symlink: a link to another case; dir: a folder).",
 "cases": [
  {
   "file": "valid-full.md",
   "verdict": "accept",
   "note": "every field; a `---` line in the body"
  },
  {
   "file": "valid-minimal.md",
   "verdict": "accept",
   "note": "id alone; the name is the id"
  },
  {
   "file": "valid-bom-crlf.md",
   "verdict": "accept",
   "note": "BOM and CRLF line ends"
  },
  {
   "file": "2026.md",
   "verdict": "accept",
   "note": "every scalar is text: the id is \"2026\""
  },
  {
   "file": "valid-nulls.md",
   "verdict": "accept",
   "note": "empty, ~ and null are no value, for single values and lists alike"
  },
  {
   "file": "valid-quoted-null.md",
   "verdict": "accept",
   "note": "a quoted null is text; an unquoted one in a list is dropped"
  },
  {
   "file": "valid-padded-id.md",
   "verdict": "accept",
   "note": "the id is trimmed before it is compared with the file name"
  },
  {
